  "description": "BER A-rated, state-of-the art building in an enclosed cul-de-sac, built in 2023.\n\nAn amazing location just over 2km from the city centre in a leafy community between Phibsborough and Glasnevin.\n\nCity living at its best with numerous cafes, restaurants, bars, supermarkets and shops close by.\n\nAll bills are included, i.e., electricity, super-fast Wi-Fi, refuse collection, cleaning, Sky TV and Netflix. There are no further utility costs, just one monthly payment. \n\nAll suites are spacious and fully furnished with a private en-suite and the benefits of a separate large kitchen / dining area and living room. \n\nWalking distance to buses, Luas and Drumcondra train station. \n\nHeat recovery systems provide a continuous fresh clean filtered air supply for a dust and allergy free environment for a healthier standard of living.\n\nFlexible license terms with 12 months or longer agreements but only one month's notice is required if your circumstances change. \n\nAll suites have access to a private garden with outdoor seating and maintenance-free all-weather artificial grass.\n \nCar parking and storage for bicycles available.\n\nFeatures:\n- Large kitchen / dining / community space \n- High specification kitchen with 2 hobs and 2 ovens \n- Individual fridge and larder for each resident \n- Stone worktops and high-quality appliances \n- Full laundry room with 2 washers, 2 dryers and ironing \n- Living Room with large screen connected to sky tv, netflix and internet. Dedicated high speed fibre going into each house with IT company hired to manage service. East suite has their own user name and password. \n- Ring doorbell intercom system with smartphone connection and Ring External CCTV. \n- Individually controlled heating in every room \n- Maintenance on call \n- Modern A-rated energy-efficient houses \n- Private community in an enclosed cul-de-sac \nEach suite has the following \n- Double-sized bed \n- Spacious ensuite with walk-in shower \n- Heated towel rail and illuminated mirror \n- Separate heating controls per room for your own comfort\n- Built-in wardrobes & clever storage \n- Sofa and coffee table \n- Work space with comfortable chair. Dedicated high speed fibre broadband with each suite having their own user name and password for secure VPN sign in when working remotely. \n- Ample storage \n\nSituated just over 2km from the city centre, residents will find commuting or just a trip into town simplicity itself. With walking to IFSC or town taking less than 25 minutes, and cycling even quicker, commutes don't come much more convenient. The area is very well served by public transport too. The Luas takes just 12 minutes from Phibsborough to George's Dock, plus there are also direct bus routes to the City Centre, Rathmines, Grangegorman and Donnybrook from the area or Drumcondra Train Station is a short walk away. If you are heading away, it's a mere 20 minutes (10km) drive from Daneswell Place to Dublin Airport.\n\nGlasnevin is one of Dublin's most historic and long-established communities and, not only does it offer fine parklands and local colleges, but it also has all the amenities and excitement of the city centre less than 25 minutes' walk away. With the perfect mix of contemporary city living and suburban calm, it's no surprise that this neighbourhood is one of the city's most desirable and sought-after locations.",
